{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789322187,"nonce":"sOSNjLUhZ20Wfh9kzdcbbdUwFkk=","title":"An indirect callee was not an operand: OSR missed it as a live-in, replace_uses left it stale","message":"`HirInstruction::Call { callee: HirCallable::Indirect(v) }` reads `v`, but `HirInstruction::operands()` and `replace_uses()` listed only the arguments, and `osr::instruction_uses` kept its own field list that left out both the indirect callee and a `CallClosure`'s closure. A function pointer or closure computed before a loop and called inside it was therefore not carried into the OSR helper (the helper read an unmapped value), and a pass renaming values through `replace_uses` left the callee pointing at the old id.\n\nFixed: `operands()` and `replace_uses()` include the indirect callee; `osr::instruction_uses` restricts the instruction kinds a helper body may contain and takes their operands from `operands()` rather than a second list. The passes that already special-cased the indirect callee (alloca_promote, aggregate_split, drop_insert) are unchanged.","files":null}]}